  "ms-learning/quick-reference-microservices-at-a-glance": {
    "title": "Quick Reference: Microservices at a Glance",
    "root": {
      "kind": "root",
      "title": "Quick Reference: Microservices at a Glance",
      "hLevel": 0,
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "summary",
          "title": "Before diving into the phases, here's the big picture.",
          "hLevel": 5,
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "kind": "sub",
          "title": "What Are Microservices?",
          "hLevel": 2,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "summary",
              "title": "Microservices are an architectural approach to developing software applications as a collection of small, independent services that communicate with each other over",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Instead of building a monolithic application where all functionality is tightly integrated into a single codebase, microservices break the application into smaller, loosely coupled services.",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Each service acts as a mini-application on its own — it can be written in different languages and frameworks.",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Each microservice is designed to perform a specific business function and can be developed, deployed, and scaled independently.",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "sub",
          "title": "Microservices vs Monolithic Architecture",
          "hLevel": 2,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "summary",
              "title": "Table comparing Microservices, Monolithic by Structure, Teams, Scaling, Deployment",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "sub",
          "title": "Benefits",
          "hLevel": 2,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Teams can work on different microservices simultaneously",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Issues in one service do not impact others, enhancing reliability",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Each service can be scaled based on its specific needs",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "The system can quickly adapt to changing workloads",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Teams can choose the best tech stack for each microservice",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "sub",
          "title": "Challenges",
          "hLevel": 2,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Managing service communication, network latency, and data consistency can be difficult",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Decomposing an app into microservices adds complexity in development, testing, and deployment",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Network communication can lead to higher latency and complicates error handling",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "leaf",
              "title": "Maintaining consistent data across services is challenging, and distributed transactions can be complex",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "branch",
          "title": "Visual Model",
          "hLevel": 1,
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  },
